pdns (5.1.3-3.devuan5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Views bugfixes found during upstream PR review and regression testing:
    - GSQLBackend::getSOA: with views enabled, a name-only SOA lookup could
      match a variant zone instead of the base zone (base and variants share
      record names). Affected AXFR-out of zones that have variants: the
      transfer could stream variant content. Now resolves the exact domain
      (variant included) via getDomainInfo before the SOA lookup.
    - viewAddZone/viewDelZone/networkSet: guard against being called with
      views disabled (would dereference an unprepared statement).
    - viewListZones/networkList: log and skip malformed rows instead of
      silently ignoring them.

 -- voyo <voyo@swarog>  Thu, 24 Jul 2026 02:50:00 +0200

pdns (5.1.3-2.devuan5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Added CAP_VIEWS (Split-Horizon Views) support for the gpgsql backend
    (see split-horizon-gpgsql-views-plan.md), for test deployment on ns2.
    Adds "networks"/"views" tables to the gpgsql schema (migration:
    4.7.0_to_5.2.0_schema.pgsql.sql) and the gpgsql-views setting.
    Not enabled by default (gpgsql-views=no) - existing zones/behaviour
    are unaffected unless explicitly turned on.

 -- voyo <voyo@swarog>  Fri, 10 Jul 2026 00:07:16 +0200

pdns (5.1.3-1.devuan5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Custom build for Devuan 5 daedalus (no-ip.pl NS upgrade, 4.7.3 -> 5.1.3).
  * Removed systemd/libsystemd-dev Build-Depends and --enable-systemd
    configure flag: Devuan has no systemd, pdns-server on ns1/ns2 is
    started via a hand-maintained /etc/init.d/pdns script instead.

 -- voyo <voyo@swarog>  Sun, 05 Jul 2026 22:14:02 +0200
